          "id": "3834cf2fda96c88e86d86c1f1ca0608c564d6301",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: keep portal events off physical ancestors that are not on the logical chain (#1370)\n\n## What & why\n\nPortal content is attached under the portal's target element, so UI Toolkit's native dispatch also runs the Velvet `events:` handlers of every physical ancestor of that content. That includes the target container itself, even when it is not a logical ancestor of the `V.Portal` call site. React is different. `accumulateSinglePhaseListeners` and `accumulateTwoPhaseListeners` in `DOMPluginEventSystem.js` walk only the fiber `return` chain, so a portal's container never hears its content's events.\n\n**The change:**\n- **`FiberCrossPanelEventDispatcher.OffLogicalChain`** decides whether an element is on the event target's logical chain. It walks from the target through each bridged context's portal relocation (`RelocatedParent`): a portal row maps to its placeholder, and a z-layer member maps to its placeholder.\n  - The set of bridged contexts is process-wide, so a portal from one mount into an element another mount rendered is gated too.\n  - A target that has already left the panel counts as on the chain. A handler that removes its own element therefore does not silence its logical ancestors.\n  - A context with no portals returns early.\n- **`FiberEventBindingManager`** gates every `events:` path with it: capture, bubble, discrete pointer and key events, value change, and the TextField focus, blur and keyboard callbacks.\n- **A `Button`'s `onClick`** is decided at release, per pointer. The click is held back only when both the press and the release happened in off-chain portal content. That matches a browser, which raises the click on the common ancestor of the two. A NavigationSubmit from off-chain content is held back as well. The gate state is cleared on pool reset.\n\n**Breaking:** a portal container that relied on hearing its content's pointer, wheel, key, focus, value-change or click events has to move that handler to a logical ancestor of the `V.Portal` call site. Details are in the `breaking/` fragment.\n\n**Docs and changelog:** `portals.md` describes the dispatch rule and its exceptions, and the `V.Portal(targetId)` remarks in `V.cs` are updated. A `breaking/` fragment is added.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `PortalOffChainAncestorTests` covers bubble and capture pointer, wheel, toggle value change, a portal into a container with handlers, the Button cases (content press and release, content submit, press in content released over the Button, multi-pointer, rebound Button, leaves the tree, `Forget`/`Clear`), cross-mount, focus-in, two portals in one mount, and the static reset.\n- Characterization cases pin what must not change:\n  - an element that is both a physical and a logical ancestor runs once per phase;\n  - a ScrollView's own wheel callback still runs;\n  - a child that removes itself leaves its logical ancestor's handler running.\n- `PortalOffChainFieldSubmitTests` covers the TextField focus-out submit helper.\n- The ScrollView wheel case formerly in `SamePanelPortalClickTests` moved into the new fixture with a raw callback probe, because a Velvet `WheelBinding` on the ScrollView is now suppressed by design.\n\nCloses #1295\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
